{
 "translation": "But a word heard in the morning does not go to waste. It keeps spinning in the mind all day long, like an argument, and sometimes a person doesn't even understand its meaning, but keeps humming it. It was due to this voice taking root that in those days, when Miss Mridula Sarabhai brought back abducted women in exchange between India and Pakistan, some men from Mullah Shakur's neighborhood were ready to resettle them. Their heirs went to meet them at Chowki Kalan, outside the city. The abducted women and their relatives looked at each other for a while, and then, with bowed heads, set about rebuilding their ruined homes. Risalu, Nekiram, and Sunderlal Babu kept chanting slogans, sometimes \"Mahendra Singh Zindabad\" and sometimes \"Sohanlal Zindabad,\" and they kept chanting those slogans until their throats dried up.",
